# Dependency directories
# Both spellings on purpose: the trailing slash matches a directory, the bare
# name also catches a *symlink* called node_modules. An agent working in a
# throwaway clone symlinks it to a shared install to avoid a second npm install,
# and `git add -A` then commits that symlink — an absolute path out of somebody's
# container — straight past the slash-only rule. That happened once (#1444).
node_modules
node_modules/
jspm_packages/

# Snowpack dependency directory (https://snowpack.dev/)
web_modules/

# TypeScript cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Optional npm cache directory
.npm

