/backups/

# Generated OpenAPI description of the internal API (scripts/openapi-generate.cjs,
# npm run gen:openapi). Derived from src/app/api, so committing it would put a
# ~500 KB diff in every PR that adds or renames a route — the same churn the
# release fragments exist to avoid (releases/README.md), and a file nobody would
# review. It is a convenience artefact for inspecting the output: the server gets
# the document through next.config.js -> nextConfig.env, so nothing imports this
# file and `npx tsc --noEmit` on a fresh clone never looks for it.
/src/generated/openapi.json

# CycloneDX SBOM (scripts/generate-sbom.mjs, npm run gen:sbom). Generated on the
# runner during build-image.yml and picked up by `COPY . .`, so the image serves
# it at /sbom.cdx.json — always describing the tree that image installed. ~280 KB
# and regenerated per build, so committing it would put a large derived diff in
# every dependency PR for no review value; the licence inventory
# (docs/legal/third-party-licenses.md) is the committed, human-readable half of
# the same evidence. A local checkout simply has no /sbom.cdx.json, which is
# correct — an unstamped SBOM is not evidence of anything.
/public/sbom.cdx.json

# Raw `npm audit --json` report (scripts/check-audit.mjs, the security-audit
# workflow). Uploaded as a build artifact there; never committed.
/audit.json

# Isolated worktrees created by Claude Code's background Agent tool for
# in-progress work — internal tooling state, not a project artifact.
/.claude/worktrees/
